{title: 437 - I'm Going Home}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #437 • IM GOING HOME • L.M. with Refrain}
{lyricist: William Hunter}
{composer: William Miller}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 437}
{meta: tune IM GOING HOME}
{meta: meter L.M. with Refrain}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]My heav'nly home is bright and [C/G]fair,
[F]Nor [C]pain [F]nor death can enter there;
[C7]It's [F]glitt'ring tow'rs the sun outshine,
[F]That heav'nly mansion shall me mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Dm]I'm going [F/C]home, [C7]I'm going [F]home,
[F]I'm going home to die no [C/G]more;
[F]To die [C]no [F]more; to die no more-
[Dm]I'm going [F/C]home to [C7]die no [F]more.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]My Father's house is built on [C/G]high,
[F]Far, [C]far [F]above the starry sky;
[C7]When [F]from this earthly prison [C/G]free,
[F]That heav'nly mansion mine shall be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Let others seek a home below,
[F]Which flames devour or waves [Dm]oe'r [F/C]flow;
[C7]Be [F]mine a happier lot to [C/G]own
[F]A heav'nly mansion near the throne.
{end_of_verse}
